{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-blog-post-tsx","path":"/blog/2026-11-13--how-i-am-using-the-muse-ai-assistant/","result":{"data":{"site":{"siteMetadata":{"disqus":"edward-j-schwartz"}},"post":{"htmlAst":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recently I have been enjoying using\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"https://about.fb.com/news/2026/09/introducing-muse-personal-ai-agent/"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Muse"}]},{"type":"text","value":",\nMeta's new personal AI agent, which runs on its own dedicated virtual machine. I\nhave found a number of ways it has been helpful to me, both as a researcher and\nin my personal life. Here are some of those stories."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The useful stuff, it turns out, is mostly things that repeat. A weekly job takes\nsome setup, but once it is set up, it mostly takes care of itself. Much of this\npost was drafted while driving, as one story below shows."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"h1","properties":{"id":"research-work","style":"position:relative;"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"#research-work","ariaLabel":"research work permalink","className":["anchor","before"]},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"svg","properties":{"ariaHidden":"true","focusable":"false","height":"16","version":"1.1","viewBox":"0 0 16 16","width":"16"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"path","properties":{"fillRule":"evenodd","d":"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z"},"children":[]}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"Research work"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"h2","properties":{"id":"paper-triage","style":"position:relative;"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"#paper-triage","ariaLabel":"paper triage permalink","className":["anchor","before"]},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"svg","properties":{"ariaHidden":"true","focusable":"false","height":"16","version":"1.1","viewBox":"0 0 16 16","width":"16"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"path","properties":{"fillRule":"evenodd","d":"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z"},"children":[]}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"Paper triage"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Since the advent of AI, I receive more notifications about new papers \"I might\nbe interested in\" than ever! When new papers arrive, Muse reads the abstracts\nfirst, so that it can summarize each paper and recommend what to do with it.\nThen we go through them together, and I decide what action to take on each one,\nif any: file it in Mendeley, add a reading todo, or just ignore it."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"h2","properties":{"id":"library-organization","style":"position:relative;"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"#library-organization","ariaLabel":"library organization permalink","className":["anchor","before"]},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"svg","properties":{"ariaHidden":"true","focusable":"false","height":"16","version":"1.1","viewBox":"0 0 16 16","width":"16"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"path","properties":{"fillRule":"evenodd","d":"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z"},"children":[]}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"Library organization"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"My paper library lives in Mendeley, and is split between personal libraries and\nlibraries shared with research colleagues. It's easy for things to get misfiled\nand duplicated. Muse helps keep my library organized. It suggests locations for\nnew papers, and a periodic audit proposes ways to restructure the library, which\nI rarely have time to think about myself."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"I have also been thinking about switching from Mendeley to Zotero, and one of\nthe things stopping me has been the difficulty of transferring my data. Muse\nmirrors my changes across both, which solves that problem completely."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"h2","properties":{"id":"email-triage","style":"position:relative;"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"#email-triage","ariaLabel":"email triage permalink","className":["anchor","before"]},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"svg","properties":{"ariaHidden":"true","focusable":"false","height":"16","version":"1.1","viewBox":"0 0 16 16","width":"16"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"path","properties":{"fillRule":"evenodd","d":"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z"},"children":[]}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"Email triage"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"I receive a lot of messages that need some kind of decision or action from me.\nWhen I'm busy, these pile up in my inbox. I have a weekly job that looks at\nemails older than a few days and attempts to triage them:"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"ul","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"li","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Many emails are "},{"type":"element","tagName":"em","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"de facto"}]},{"type":"text","value":" todo items that I keep until the task is done. For\nthese, it suggests archiving the email and adding a todo item."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"li","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Many are notifications about new papers and the like. For these, it suggests\nfiling them, or disregarding them if they don't seem relevant to me."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Because it knows what is going on in my life, it often makes reasonable\nsuggestions. It can also write draft responses, unsubscribe from spammy mailing\nlists, and more."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"h2","properties":{"id":"waiting-and-monitoring","style":"position:relative;"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"#waiting-and-monitoring","ariaLabel":"waiting and monitoring permalink","className":["anchor","before"]},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"svg","properties":{"ariaHidden":"true","focusable":"false","height":"16","version":"1.1","viewBox":"0 0 16 16","width":"16"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"path","properties":{"fillRule":"evenodd","d":"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z"},"children":[]}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"Waiting and monitoring"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Muse is really good at waiting and monitoring, which is especially useful when\ndelegating. When I hand something to another person, Muse waits for evidence\nthat the task was completed. For example, I recently asked someone at work to\nschedule a trip for me. Sometimes balls get dropped, so I asked Muse to keep\ntrack of it. It checks for emails about the trip, and if none arrive in a couple\nof days, it lets me know. If one does arrive, I don't need to hear or think\nabout it, which is the whole point."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Another example: I recently received a notification about a paper,\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.29566"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"VMSpec"}]},{"type":"text","value":". I was very interested in the\nimplementation, which the paper said would be released. So I asked Muse to watch\nfor the release and notify me when it comes out. (On the personal side, it can\nalso watch for good prices on items I want to buy.)"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"h1","properties":{"id":"driving","style":"position:relative;"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"#driving","ariaLabel":"driving permalink","className":["anchor","before"]},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"svg","properties":{"ariaHidden":"true","focusable":"false","height":"16","version":"1.1","viewBox":"0 0 16 16","width":"16"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"path","properties":{"fillRule":"evenodd","d":"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z"},"children":[]}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"Driving"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Much of this post was drafted while I was driving to Pittsburgh. I talked, Muse\nwrote, and the post you are reading is the result. Driving time is normally dead\ntime, and voice turns it into productive time."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"I had positive experiences talking to an LLM while driving even before Muse. One\nexample is "},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"/blog/2026-05-28--towards-the-next-generation-oo-analyzer/"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"reformulating OOAnalyzer as a search/optimization\nproblem"}]},{"type":"text","value":". I spent\nmost of a four-hour drive to Pittsburgh conversing with GPT about various\nframeworks for modeling problems. We eventually arrived at Answer Set\nProgramming, which is conceptually the perfect fit. A long drive can be a good\nplace to think and brainstorm, because there aren't many interruptions. (Caveat:\nI am mostly driving on the very straight PA Turnpike, which admittedly does not\nrequire my full attention.)"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"In addition to drafting this blog post, I also had Muse create podcasts about\nseveral papers that seemed interesting, and listened to them during the drive. A\npodcast is not a replacement for reading the paper, but it's good enough to get\nan understanding of the work, and to decide whether it's worth reading in full."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"h1","properties":{"id":"personal-routines","style":"position:relative;"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"#personal-routines","ariaLabel":"personal routines permalink","className":["anchor","before"]},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"svg","properties":{"ariaHidden":"true","focusable":"false","height":"16","version":"1.1","viewBox":"0 0 16 16","width":"16"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"path","properties":{"fillRule":"evenodd","d":"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z"},"children":[]}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"Personal routines"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The same repeated-work pattern shows up outside of research, too."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"h2","properties":{"id":"back-pain-logging","style":"position:relative;"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"#back-pain-logging","ariaLabel":"back pain logging permalink","className":["anchor","before"]},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"svg","properties":{"ariaHidden":"true","focusable":"false","height":"16","version":"1.1","viewBox":"0 0 16 16","width":"16"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"path","properties":{"fillRule":"evenodd","d":"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z"},"children":[]}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"Back pain logging"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"I have chronic back pain that seems to crop up without rhyme or reason. I've\nbeen collecting data on possible factors so that I can do some statistical\nmodeling. Twice a day, Muse prompts me to rate my back pain on a scale of 0\nto 4. No big deal so far. But it also fills in information about possible causes:\nweather, plus steps, sleep, and exercise data from Garmin and Health Connect.\nAll of the data is logged into a Google Sheet."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"We then worked together to develop a Bayesian statistical model to fit the data with an interative demo page."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"h2","properties":{"id":"weekends","style":"position:relative;"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"#weekends","ariaLabel":"weekends permalink","className":["anchor","before"]},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"svg","properties":{"ariaHidden":"true","focusable":"false","height":"16","version":"1.1","viewBox":"0 0 16 16","width":"16"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"path","properties":{"fillRule":"evenodd","d":"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z"},"children":[]}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"Weekends"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"On Saturdays and Sundays, Muse checks my calendar to see whether my day is\nlight, and if it is, it suggests two or three undated tasks from my backlog. It\nalso nags me to do one small thing each weekend to clean up my office. These\nlittle nudges can add up to a lot over the long term."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"h1","properties":{"id":"connectors","style":"position:relative;"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"#connectors","ariaLabel":"connectors permalink","className":["anchor","before"]},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"svg","properties":{"ariaHidden":"true","focusable":"false","height":"16","version":"1.1","viewBox":"0 0 16 16","width":"16"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"path","properties":{"fillRule":"evenodd","d":"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z"},"children":[]}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"Connectors"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"A frequent and frustrating problem is trying to use AI for a task, only to find\nthat it can't integrate with the service it needs. Muse has two features for\ndealing with this. First, it can run a real browser, which lets it interact with\nmost web-based services. Second, and even cooler, Muse can build its own\nconnectors. For example, Muse did not have connectors for Mendeley or Zotero, so\nit built its own using those services' developer APIs. This is a godsend, and in\nhindsight an obvious killer feature for agents that can write code."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Of course, handing over your credentials to an AI agent is a concerning\nproposition. We all remember the horror stories from the early days of OpenClaw,\nsuch as the "},{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"https://techcrunch.com/2026/02/23/a-meta-ai-security-researcher-said-an-openclaw-agent-ran-amok-on-her-inbox/"},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"agent that deleted hundreds of a user's\nemails"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\ndespite being told to ask first. Muse has an elegant design for avoiding this\nproblem. Credentials and tokens are stored separately and are never provided to\nthe LLM itself. Instead, the LLM is given temporary opaque tokens, which are\nswapped for the real ones as requests leave Muse's VM. That swap point is also\nwhere Muse enforces policy-based controls. Since the LLM never sees your real\ncredentials, it can't bypass the gate. I like this design a lot."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"h1","properties":{"id":"conclusion","style":"position:relative;"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"#conclusion","ariaLabel":"conclusion permalink","className":["anchor","before"]},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"svg","properties":{"ariaHidden":"true","focusable":"false","height":"16","version":"1.1","viewBox":"0 0 16 16","width":"16"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"path","properties":{"fillRule":"evenodd","d":"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z"},"children":[]}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"Conclusion"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"I've found a lot of value in Muse, even though the model itself is not quite as powerful as frontier LLMs. Hopefully this post gives you some ideas for how\nMuse or another assistant could help in your life too!"}]}],"data":{"quirksMode":false}},"excerpt":"Recently I have been enjoying using\nMuse,\nMeta's new personal AI agent, which runs on its own dedicated virtual machine. I\nhave found a…","timeToRead":4,"fields":{"slug":"/blog/2026-11-13--how-i-am-using-the-muse-ai-assistant/"},"frontmatter":{"tags":["ai","llm"],"author":{"jsonId":"Edward J. Schwartz","bio":"Computer Security Researcher","twitter":"@edmcman","avatar":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"fixed","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/png;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/4ed6d/ed.png","srcSet":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/4ed6d/ed.png 80w","sizes":"80px"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/1deab/ed.webp 80w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"80px"}]},"width":80,"height":80}}}},"title":"How I Am Using the Muse AI Assistant","updatedDate":"Nov 13, 2026","image":null}},"recents":{"edges":[{"node":{"id":"76b23f92-df19-5c35-8638-22d1f45aa81c","fields":{"slug":"/blog/2026-10-04--more-thoughts-on-verification-of-decompilation/"},"timeToRead":4,"frontmatter":{"title":"More Rough Thoughts on Verification of Decompilation: Comparing Memory Instead of Arguments","image":null,"author":{"jsonId":"Edward J. Schwartz","avatar":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"fixed","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/png;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/8ef0e/ed.png","srcSet":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/8ef0e/ed.png 36w,\n/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/b0e74/ed.png 72w","sizes":"36px"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/stati